{
  "_about": "BIOMEDRESS: per-zone scenery dressing painted from the owner's 2D concept art (docs/reference/biome-concept-*.webp, specs 26-28). One entry per BIOMEZONES zone id. Each zone lists the kinds it grows, with a density per m2 of that zone on the island. A kind names sprites from data/world/sprites2d.json (never a hard-coded path), the zones it may grow in (a kind placed outside its list is a wrong-biome bug), how it is placed (where: ground = soil, edge = water margin, water = channel/shallow, rock = rock/ash/cliff or steep, coast = sand or a couple of metres from it, any = any dry ground), a per-kind clump (how many cards per spot) and spread (metres), and a tint that pushes the shared sheet art to the biome's palette. The concept art is the target: reed beds and lily pads along water, plume grass, termite mounds and aloes on savanna, red sandstone and blue crystals on canyon, black basalt/obsidian and sulphur on volcanic, palms/ferns/bromeliads on tropical.",
  "min_zone_tiles": 40,
  "min_instances_per_kind": 3,
